      "text": "To find the value of \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\) where \\(r\\), \\(s\\), and \\(t\\) are the roots of the polynomial equation \\(x^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7 = 0\\), we will use Vieta's formulas and algebraic manipulation.\n\nFirst, recall Vieta's formulas for the polynomial \\(x^3 + px^2 + qx + r = 0\\). For the polynomial \\(x^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7 = 0\\), we identify:\n- The sum of the roots \\(r + s + t = -(-20) = 20\\),\n- The sum of the product of the roots taken two at a time \\(rs + rt + st = 18\\),\n- The product of the roots \\(rst = -(-7) = 7\\).\n\nWe need to find the value of \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\). First, expand the expression \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\):\n\\[\n(1+r)(1+s)(1+t) = 1 + r + s + t + rs + rt + st + rt + st + rst.\n\\]\nSimplify the expression by combining like terms:\n\\[\n(1+r)(1+s)(1+t) = 1 + (r+s+t) + (rs+rt+st) + rst.\n\\]\nSubstitute the values given by Vieta's formulas:\n\\[\n1 + (r+s+t) + (rs+rt+st) + rst = 1 + 20 + 18 + 7.\n\\]\nCalculate the sum:\n\\[\n1 + 20 + 18 + 7 = 46.\n\\]\nTherefore, the value of \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\) is \\(\\boxed{46}\\).",
